# Normalise line endings in the repository, so a checkout on Windows and one on
# Linux produce identical behaviour.
* text=auto

# Email fixtures are wire-format samples, not source code. Git must not rewrite
# their line endings on checkout: a fixture that is LF on the author's disk and
# CRLF on a fresh clone makes the parser tests pass in one place and fail in the
# other, which is exactly what happened once and took a clean-clone run to find.
*.eml -text

# Calendar files are likewise a wire format (RFC 5545 requires CRLF).
*.ics -text
